{
  "recommendation": "For your $5,000 balance, the most practical combination is a Gold Account savings account plus a Gold Rewards Card, while keeping your existing Light Blue checking account.",
  "why": [
    "The Gold Account has a 5.5% base APY.",
    "A Gold Rewards Card reduces the Gold Account minimum balance requirement from $10,000 to $5,000.",
    "The Gold Rewards Card adds a 0.025% APY relationship bonus, for an effective APY of approximately 5.525%.",
    "At a constant $5,000 balance, that would produce approximately $276.25 over one year before any card fee or taxes.",
    "Your Light Blue checking account does not appear in the documented qualifying checking-and-savings pairings, so it would not add a linked-account APY boost."
  ],
  "important_tradeoff": {
    "EcoCard": "The EcoCard offers a larger +0.6% bonus on a Gold Account, but it does not provide the documented reduction of the Gold Account minimum balance. With only $5,000, you would generally not meet the standard $10,000 requirement. It also has a $50 annual fee.",
    "credit_card_interest": "Any interest or fees from carrying a credit-card balance could easily outweigh the savings interest. To maximize net earnings, pay the card balance in full each month.",
    "bonus_stacking": "Credit-card APY bonuses do not stack; only the highest applicable card bonus applies."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "I could not find the Gold Rewards Card annual fee or its standard cash-back rate in the available product documentation, so I cannot calculate the exact net return after card fees.",
    "The savings documentation also does not clearly state a Gold Account maintenance fee. Confirm those terms before applying."
  ],
  "next_step": "If you tell me whether you expect to pay the credit card in full each month and how much you expect to spend on it, I can compare the likely rewards against the card fee and estimate a more precise one-year net result."
}

{
